  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1802.17 Significant aquatic habitat",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1802.17 “Significant aquatic habitat” means regions which are important to the survival of particular aquatic populations. Such regions include, but are not limited to, spawning beds and feeding areas.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1800) #8326, eff 4-21-05; ss by #9330, eff 11-26-08 (from Env-Wq 1802.16); renumbered by #9657 (from Env-Wq 1802.16); ss by #12185, eff 5-25-17",
